<title>DENMARK: Unidanmark sells Copenhagen properties.</title>
<headline>Unidanmark sells Copenhagen properties.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's second biggest bank Unidanmark said on Friday it sold five properties in central Copenhagen to the local ATP pension fund for a total price of 315 million crowns.</p>
<p>&quot;The sale is part of Unidanmark's policy to lower its property portfolio. The purchase price was a little higher than book value, so the deal will bring in the bank a small extraordinary income,&quot; Unidanmark said in a statement.</p>
<p>ATP - the Danish Labour Market's Supplementary Pension Fund - is the largest institutional investor in Denmark. --Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
